## Status: SCAFFOLD

This directory was **generated**. Nothing in it has been built, tested, audited
or deployed. Its existence is not evidence that any capability described in it
exists, is correct, or is operational.

## The one rule

> **The catalog says a file exists. It does not expose its contents.**

Every file in the source tree is recorded in `CATALOG/` with full metadata. No
file content is copied into this layout unless an operator explicitly asks for
it, and the CLI refuses by default.

## Layout

| Directory | Holds | Populated by |
|---|---|---|
| `CATALOG/` | Complete metadata inventory of the source tree | `melodie catalog --build` |
| `SOURCE/` | Explicitly extracted file content | `melodie extract` (deny-by-default, audited) |
| `DOCS/` | Approved documentation | Operator decision |
| `TESTS/` | Test suites that pass in *this* environment | Operator decision |
| `WEB3/` | Sanitized Web3 implementation | `melodie init --template web3` |
| `ARCHITECTURE/` | Architecture specifications | Operator decision |
| `PUBLISHING/` | Packaging and release configuration | Operator decision |

`SOURCE/` ships **empty** on purpose. An empty directory is the correct state
for a template, not a missing feature.

## Verify this layout is intact

```bash
melodie verify            # catalog integrity + secret-leak scan
melodie verify --deep     # also re-hash every source file and compare
melodie status            # capability status with evidence
```

## Extract content (deny by default)

```bash
# see what exists, without reading any content
melodie inspect --category SOURCE
melodie inspect "wallet"

# decide first, write nothing
melodie extract "some/file.ts" --dry-run

# actually copy
melodie extract "some/file.ts" --out ./SOURCE
```

Credential material is **permanently** denied. No flag unlocks it. Other
excluded categories require `--i-have-authorization`, and every decision is
written to `SOURCE/extract-audit.jsonl`.

## Web3

`WEB3/` is a pointer, not an implementation. To generate a read-only wallet
application:

```bash
melodie init ./WEB3/app --template web3
```

That produces a read-only application. It will not generate a private key, hold
custody, sign, or broadcast anything unless you explicitly ask for the
signing code and accept responsibility for it.

